{#-
  schema-version-nav.njk — shared schema-format version navigation for the
  schema reference docs.

  The including page sets `schemaDocVersion` in its front matter (e.g. v0.3).
  The navigation lists schema format versions current-first and, on
  non-current versions, renders a maintenance notice.

  Entry hrefs follow three rules:
    1. The entry for the including page's own version always links to the
       page itself and carries aria-current="page".
    2. The counterpart entry links to the published sibling page when the
       including page provides the matching override: schemaDocV04Href for
       the v0.4 entry, schemaDocV03Href for the v0.3 entry.
    3. Otherwise the counterpart entry falls back to the schema overview
       (/docs/schemas/). On a v0.4 page with no v0.3 sibling the v0.3 entry
       is not linked and reads "not in this version". This partial must never invent /docs/schemas/v0.4/... or
       /docs/schemas/v0.3/... URLs for reference pages that do not exist
       yet.

  Published sibling pairs so far: v0.3 dtcg-extensions <-> v0.4
  dtcg-extensions, v0.3 tokens <-> v0.4 tokens, v0.3 utilities <-> v0.4
  utilities, and v0.3 components <-> v0.4 components (mapped in both
  directions via the overrides). The v0.4 icons and lifecycle pages have no
  v0.3 siblings, so their v0.3 entries read "not in this version". When a
  missing sibling page is published, add its override to the including
  page's front matter (and update scripts/schema-version-nav.test.mjs).
-#}
{%- if schemaDocVersion == 'v0.4' %}
{#- v0.4 page: own entry links to this page; v0.3 entry uses the sibling override or the overview fallback. -#}
{%- set v04Href = page.url -%}
{%- set v04Fallback = false -%}
{%- set v03Href = schemaDocV03Href or '/docs/schemas/' -%}
{%- set v03Fallback = not schemaDocV03Href -%}
{%- elif schemaDocVersion == 'v0.3' %}
{#- v0.3 page: v0.4 entry uses the sibling override or the overview fallback; own entry links to this page. -#}
{%- set v04Href = schemaDocV04Href or '/docs/schemas/' -%}
{%- set v04Fallback = not schemaDocV04Href -%}
{%- set v03Href = page.url -%}
{%- set v03Fallback = false -%}
{%- else %}
{#- Unversioned page: both entries use the sibling override or the overview fallback. -#}
{%- set v04Href = schemaDocV04Href or '/docs/schemas/' -%}
{%- set v04Fallback = not schemaDocV04Href -%}
{%- set v03Href = schemaDocV03Href or '/docs/schemas/' -%}
{%- set v03Fallback = not schemaDocV03Href -%}
{%- endif %}
{%- set versions = [
  { version: 'v0.4', status: 'current', href: v04Href, unavailable: false },
  { version: 'v0.3', status: 'previous', href: v03Href, unavailable: v03Fallback and schemaDocVersion == 'v0.4' }
] -%}
<aside class="schema-version-nav">
  {%- if schemaDocVersion and schemaDocVersion != 'v0.4' %}
  <p class="schema-version-nav__notice">
    <strong>Previous version:</strong> this reference documents schema format
    <code>{{ schemaDocVersion }}</code>, which is kept for compatibility.
    The current and default format is
    <a href="{{ schemaDocV04Href or '/docs/schemas/' }}">v0.4</a>
    {%- if schemaDocV04Href %}. The v0.4 entry links to this reference's successor page.{% else %}. Published v0.4 reference pages are listed on the schema overview, so the v0.4 entry links there.{% endif %}
  </p>
  {%- endif %}
  <nav class="schema-version-nav__list" aria-label="Schema format versions">
    <ul>
      {%- for entry in versions %}
      {%- if entry.unavailable %}
      <li><span class="schema-version-nav__missing">{{ entry.version }}<span class="schema-version-nav__status">not in this version</span></span></li>
      {%- else %}
      <li><a href="{{ entry.href }}"{% if entry.version == schemaDocVersion %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ entry.version }}<span class="schema-version-nav__status">{{ entry.status }}</span></a></li>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </nav>
</aside>
